  "_comment": "Building pieces (D121). B opens building: number keys pick a category, V cycles its shapes, X its materials (roofs: logs or thatch), R / the wheel turns it, the left mouse places a blueprint, E brings materials from the pack, the middle mouse (or Backspace) takes a piece down. Coordinates in metres, Y up, the piece's own axes (its model's: Blender's -Y is +Z here). box = centre x y z, half-size x y z (overlaps are checked within a group); snap = points it joins other pieces by (a joint where points meet), attach = the groups whose points it joins (a roof rests on walls and roofs, not on floors); ground = may stand on the bare ground, its origin lifted by lift, its legs reaching down legs metres; cost = what its blueprint needs; joins = the points it joins others by when it is placed (floors: their outer edges only; default: all its snap points); edges = lines walls and stairs attach to (x1 y1 z1 x2 y2 z2); family + length: the walls of one shape in their sizes (the edge picks the size; smaller = the family to use on an edge too short, a narrow piece slots into halves of a longer edge); edge = how it attaches (wall: centred on the edge; stairs: its top on it). Grid 3 m; walls 3 m high; steep roofs 45°, low ones 26.6°.",
